		<defName>Anneli_Faction_YoRHa</defName>
		<label>Anneli Faction YoRHa Butai</label>
		<description>Long ago, in a quiet place far away, lived the annelitrice.\nOne day, they found a forgotten library filled with stories about the greatness of mankind.\nOne of them told of heroes called YoRHa, who fought for something precious called Humanity.\n\nThe annelitrice loved the story, and they loved Humans very much.\nThey stitched black uniforms for themselves, learned the forgotten salutes, and practiced the old ways of fighting.\n"We will go into the wide world," they promised, "and we will help Humans."\n\nThey did not have to search long. \nThe first human asked for beer. \nThe second asked for silver. \nThe third wished to destroy bandits. \nThe fourth wanted his neighbor’s land. \nThe fifth wanted the fourth gone. \nThe sixth demanded complete obedience. \nThe annelitrice served them all. \nWere these the Humans from the stories? \nProbably not. \nPerhaps they were humans—but not yet Humanity. \n\nSo they crossed burning deserts and pale oceans. \nAt last, in the shadow of a rusted factory, they found a strange machine. \nIt was built long ago to pack food into cans. \nNo one knew who made it. \nNo one knew why it was wrapped in fresh human skin.\nThe machine rarely spoke. \nBut whenever the hungry came, it offered food. \nIt fed every creature, without condition or question. \nAh, thought the annelitrice. \nHere, at last, was a Humanity.\n\nAnd so, feeling hopeful once more, they continued their search.</description>
